cast:
  Zofia:
  Grace:
  Ollie:
  Mara:
  Ruth:
  Kit:
  Ewa:
  Will:
  Hale:
~~~~
exception
---
Ruth: Zofia, visitor agreement, read the last paragraph.
Zofia: One sitting. Escorted entry and exit. No extra rooms. I've read it.
Ruth: Grace, your copy too. Mara requested an exception. This is the exception.
Grace: Does the response debate count as an extra room or an extra day?
Ruth: It requires another decision.
Mara: Zofia, I will ask for that visit when we have a date. Today we have the preliminary response. I wanted the whole answer today. I couldn't get it.
Zofia: The petition. They have it. Why can't they just answer?
Mara: Because naming the office that has a record isn't the same as searching the record. Today I want names and dates said publicly. Then we can ask why a named person missed a named date.
Grace: We already sent names and dates.
Mara: You did. They ignored you. That is the correspondence I have asked the minister to address.
Zofia: So I sit still while somebody reads out that nobody answered us.
Mara: And while somebody has to say what happens next. You can hate how long it took. Please listen for what they actually promise.
Ruth: Zofia, agreement, sign if you accept it.
Zofia: If I don't?
Ruth: You do not enter under this arrangement.
Grace: There. At least that answer arrived on time.

on-the-table
---
Zofia: The Mace. On the Table. Can you hear?
Hale: Madam, if this be the appointed hearing, I attend; let the undertaking be spoken before its limits are concealed. [class=dead]
Zofia: Hale can hear. He's already annoyed.
Grace: Good. He's caught up with the rest of us.
Will: Mistress, the paper with the cases first. You have set the wet bottle against its edge. [class=dead]
Zofia: It's shut.
Will: A flour sack likewise appears sound until the bottom gives. Set it beneath the seat, if you please. [class=dead]
Zofia: Fine. Bottle down.
Grace: But why do we still do this? The chair held you hostage at rehearsal; now this stick decides whether he counts as a witness.
Kit: Without it he only has Zofia's report. Today he can hear for himself. You wanted that too.
Grace: Yes. And Ruth can decide we don't come back. Am I supposed to defend a ceremony I'm allowed into as a favour?
Kit: I can't promise another visit. Wait. I can ask for the next decision in writing, with a reason. I'll put my name on the request.
Grace: Send it to us as well. Dad shouldn't have to chase you after his shift.
Kit: I will.
Grace: And before you go, tell Zofia which end of that case you watched. She keeps staring at it.
Kit: At the end. Remind me before we move.

what-was-promised
---
Zofia: The date. Did she say the debate has a date?
Grace: Yes. And that the Association has to be asked for its search, not told what result to find.
Hale: If my reason is to be entered, madam, ask whether the entry shall undo the judgment; I will not have the smaller remedy smuggled in beneath the greater word. [class=dead]
Zofia: Hale wants to know if recording his reason reverses the judgment.
Grace: We knew he'd ask that.
Zofia: I wanted him to hear someone with the actual job say it.
Hale: Then let that person speak, and not this present arrangement of messengers speaking of messengers. [class=dead]
Zofia: She's saying the office will identify the account and reply about its policy. Not change the judgment. Not today.
Hale: If an office promises only to declare its policy, it has not promised to hear my cause. I grant the distinction, madam; I do not grant satisfaction. [class=dead]
Zofia: I know. I wanted more too.
Grace: Good. Write down the limit too.
Will: Mistress, beside that, the long case. Count what you saw before the bustle drives it from your head. [class=dead]
Zofia: The equipment case?
Will: Aye. How many men at either end, and which bore the weight? A master may command a delivery without once laying hand upon the sack. [class=dead]
Zofia: One question at a time. You're worse than my maths teacher.
Will: If your reckoning master lets a missing measure pass, mistress, I should ask another to weigh my flour. [class=dead]

reply
---
Zofia: The Workshop. They've replied.
Grace: Another receipt?
Zofia: No. The editor's name. An actual name at the bottom.
Will: Mistress, read the charge first, lest they answer one they were never asked. [class=dead]
Zofia: It's attached. I'll start there.

read-correction
---
Zofia: “We accept responsibility.” They've actually put that.
Will: And the stranger, mistress? No other man's name beneath the charge to clear my master's? [class=dead]
Zofia: No. You heard the bit about Hubert. Do you want me to read it again?
Will: I heard, mistress. [class=dead]
Zofia: They haven't said he couldn't have done it. Your master.
Will: They have weighed what they laid against him. Leave the two leaves together, mistress; a baker keeps the spoiled batch in his reckoning. About the case, I would count— [class=dead]

ask-once
---
Zofia: Will?
Grace: Zofia?
Zofia: He was going to tell me what to count.
Grace: The case?
Zofia: Yes.
Grace: Can you still hear the others?
Zofia: Yes.
Hale: Madam, I remain; if his answer has been delivered, no summons of ours can bind him to attend again. [class=dead]
Zofia: Will? I haven't closed it.
Grace: Do you want me to put the reply away?
Zofia: No. If I close it I'll have to open it again.
Grace: All right.
Zofia: I thought we'd finish the list first.
Grace: We can finish it.
Zofia: I can't remember which end Samuel said.
Grace: Then leave that space. Ask Samuel. We don't fill it because Will can't.

last-question
---
Kit: One minute. They're nearly finished. I can pass a request down, or answer about the case. Then I have to move.
Zofia: Hale wants the date said again.
Hale: If the appointed hour has expired, madam, record that I asked within it. I shall not have their rising entered as my consent. [class=dead]
Zofia: He says leaving isn't agreeing.
Grace: Neither is sitting still. But Will asked about that case. If Kit goes, who do we ask?
Kit: Choose now. Mara can speak to you afterwards. He won't hear that part himself.

date-first
---
Zofia: The date. Please ask now.
Kit: Right. Stay here. I'll pass it down.
Grace: The case?
Zofia: After. We'll have to catch him after.

case-first
---
Zofia: Which end of the case? Before you go.
Kit: The near end. I was beside it. I checked the time, then—
Grace: Then what?
Kit: They're rising. Keep the aisle clear.
Zofia: Wait. The date—

after-rising
---
Zofia: Hale?
Hale: Madam, I am beside you; the member's words are no longer within my hearing. Do not enter that absence as a refusal to listen. [class=dead]
Zofia: He's out here. Still with me. He didn't hear the end.
Grace: You did.
Zofia: It's not the same.
Grace: I know. Tell him what you heard.

relay-date
---
Zofia: Mara. Could you say the date again? I was writing something down.
Mara: Here. This date, on the paper. The later debate is for the searches and replies. I still haven't got you a promise to reverse his judgment.
Zofia: Hale, she says the date stands. The searches and replies. No reversal promised.

still-arguing
---
Zofia: They never got to the reasons. I'll check the written reply.
Hale: Then carry the missing words faithfully, madam. I shall dispute the remedy, not a sentence supplied to please me. [class=dead]
Zofia: He'll keep arguing.
Grace: Then we haven't lost everybody.

reconciliation
---
Ruth: Kit, dispatch sheet, bring it here. Zofia, stay beside Grace.
Kit: The dispatch, then the return. Except the return isn't—I'll get the sheet.
Zofia: The case. Why is that one coming back empty?
Ruth: Inventory reconciliation. Nobody follows it.
Zofia: Where's the Mace?
Ruth: Zofia, position, stay there.
Kit: I didn't see a diversion. I saw the case go through. That's all.
Zofia: I didn't ask about a diversion.
Kit: I mean, I didn't see it leave the route. I was checking the time.
Ruth: Kit, written account, before you leave.
Zofia: You haven't got it back.
Ruth: The return has not been confirmed.
Grace: That wasn't her question.
Ruth: Grace, the holding room is locked. You will not enter it. Neither will Zofia.
Zofia: I'm not asking to go in. I'm asking you to say what's missing.
Ruth: The Mace has not been accounted for after transfer.
Zofia: Then put that on the sheet.
Ruth: I will record the incident.
Zofia: Not reconciliation.
Ruth: Zofia, enough.

old-time
---
Ollie: Right, so inventory reconciliation could mean an interdepartmental object alignment, which sounds better, until you ask where the object—
Ewa: The paper. Give it here.
Ollie: I was trying to help.
Ewa: Give me something I can read.
Zofia: This time. Fourteen forty. That's on the rehearsal copy Morwenna showed us.
Ewa: What date is on this one?
Zofia: Week four. Tuesday. Today.
Ewa: And beside my name?
Zofia: Fourteen hundred to eighteen hundred. Same route and time. It says staff access requires examination.
Ewa: I did not work that shift today.
Zofia: Then this proves—
Ewa: It proves what somebody wrote. Get the roster. Get the original entry. My saying it is wrong does not make this paper disappear.
Ollie: Why is a Polish girl doing Britain's paperwork anyway?
Zofia: Hubert. That's why. A foreign name gets stuck to something, and then everybody looks at the name instead of what happened.
Ollie: I meant you shouldn't have to. Not that you shouldn't be here.
Zofia: Then say that. Mum's name is on this. I'm here.
Ewa: My name, my shift. Ask me about it before you defend me to a corridor full of people.
Zofia: Sorry. Can we get your roster?
Ewa: Yes. A copy with my name on it. And the original log that this claims to follow.
Ollie: I told Vale the Mace had to be genuine. After the test. I thought he was asking because he carried equipment.
Zofia: I know you told him.
Ollie: I'm telling your mum too.
Ewa: Then write whom you told, and when. Do not improve the wording.

exception-withdrawn
---
Zofia: The original log. We need to compare this with it.
Ruth: Ewa, written correction, submit it to me. I will check the shifts.
Ewa: I will submit my shift. You will retain the original you check it against.
Ruth: Yes.
Zofia: And show us which entry supplied fourteen forty.
Ruth: The discrepancy has been reported. Your access under the one-visit exception is finished.
Zofia: You were going to decide about the debate.
Ruth: I have decided. No further visit under my exception.
Grace: Because she asked for the paper? Kit requested a written decision. Put that reason beside his name.
Ruth: Because the conditions of this arrangement have broken down. You will leave with your escort.
Zofia: If I say reconciliation, do we get to come back?
Ewa: Zofia.
Zofia: No. I want the log request kept. With today's date. Even if we can't come back.
Ruth: I will acknowledge the log request in writing. You will receive the access decision too.
Hale: Madam, if they deny you the door, retain the petition for entry; do not purchase it by surrendering the account. [class=dead]
Zofia: He says keep asking.
Ewa: We are leaving. We can ask from outside.
Zofia: Kit saw the case. He was right there.
Grace: Then Kit needs to tell us what he saw.
